# f1 = last, f2 = halves, f3 = wide, f4 = mixed. Where proofs are checked at run time (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, which --aot-harden=proof-checks stands for):
# a parameter of a loop's head that lies boxed, or as an optional integer, is asked in each iteration for what is shown of it;
# what a branch has narrowed is held also where it lies as an optional number, as it is for raw numbers: an Int64 is the third row. As users build, nothing is asked.
# RUN(HEADS): walk f1 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HEADS: ([[held]]: undefined|i32 @OptionalInt64, {{*}}isLoopHead=true:
# HEADS-NEXT: = CheckProof [[held]] checkedType=undefined|i32 {{*}}source=OtherOperation
# RUN(BOXED): walk f4 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# BOXED: ([[held]]: undefined|i32|string @JSValue, {{*}}isLoopHead=true:
# BOXED-NEXT: = CheckProof [[held]] checkedType=undefined|i32|string {{*}}source=OtherOperation
# RUN(OPTIONAL): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# OPTIONAL: [[narrowed]]: number @OptionalDouble = Narrowed
# OPTIONAL-NEXT: = CheckProof [[narrowed]] checkedType=number {{*}}source=Test
# RUN(WIDE): walk f3 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# WIDE: [[narrowed]]: int[0, 2147483647] @Int64 = Narrowed
# WIDE-NEXT: = CheckProof [[narrowed]] checkedType=int[0, 2147483647] {{*}}source=Test
# RUN(PLAIN): walk f1 f2 f3 f4 mechanisms=all
# PLAIN-NOT: source=Test
# PLAIN-NOT: source=OtherOperation
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 6 3 12.5 none 2x24
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
